t is $6\\,\\text{ft}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f2401f1c-06d1-5801-99a9-014558325a8d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f2401f1c-06d1-5801-99a9-014558325a8d" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2401f1c-06d1-5801-99a9-014558325a8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ebc6dd75-bd90-5b33-813d-0b70e4da79f4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3a4820ff-c940-5e49-ab2d-091e7242efca" "answer-f152c486-b18d-5f7c-bbda-402cea16b82b" "answer-62232616-9670-5cb6-98c2-2cdc26aec438" "answer-ebc6dd75-bd90-5b33-813d-0b70e4da79f4" "answer-e7dc7f7e-eda8-511d-a185-29c6f05793ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a4820ff-c940-5e49-ab2d-091e7242efca" :answer/id #uuid "3a4820ff-c940-5e49-ab2d-091e7242efca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f152c486-b18d-5f7c-bbda-402cea16b82b" :answer/id #uuid "f152c486-b18d-5f7c-bbda-402cea16b82b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62232616-9670-5cb6-98c2-2cdc26aec438" :answer/id #uuid "62232616-9670-5cb6-98c2-2cdc26aec438" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ebc6dd75-bd90-5b33-813d-0b70e4da79f4" :answer/id #uuid "ebc6dd75-bd90-5b33-813d-0b70e4da79f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7dc7f7e-eda8-511d-a185-29c6f05793ce" :answer/id #uuid "e7dc7f7e-eda8-511d-a185-29c6f05793ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{ft}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186419595 :answer-field/choices 17592186419590] [:db/retract 17592186419595 :answer-field/choices 17592186419591] [:db/retract 17592186419595 :answer-field/choices 17592186419592] [:db/retract 17592186419595 :answer-field/choices 17592186419593] [:db/retract 17592186419595 :answer-field/choices 17592186419594] [:db/retract 17592186284357 :answer-field/choices 17592186283588] [:db/retract 17592186284357 :answer-field/choices 17592186282181] [:db/retract 17592186284357 :answer-field/choices 17592186282645] [:db/retract 17592186284357 :answer-field/choices 17592186281915] [:db/retract 17592186284357 :answer-field/choices 17592186283308] {:db/id 17592186124506 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e09cfecd-e23b-5baa-8f4c-7e2b5c69c1a9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124502 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-be1595d6-b16a-5715-995c-d3645afe8a1e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124507 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b46dd9b0-6a80-5531-9884-f4687e775cb2" "question-15b3432d-8b0c-5d62-a84d-7dadd72f7ac7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e09cfecd-e23b-5baa-8f4c-7e2b5c69c1a9" :question/id #uuid "e09cfecd-e23b-5baa-8f4c-7e2b5c69c1a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-71945" :question/problem "What is the radius of the sphere ${x}^{2}-6x+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=17?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nBy completing the square for the variable $x$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-6x+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =17 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-6x+9)+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =17+9 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write our equation as\n\n$$\n(x-3)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=(\\sqrt{26})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us a radius of $\\sqrt{26}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-09bef14a-87dd-54de-aa74-0d9d9cab649d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-09bef14a-87dd-54de-aa74-0d9d9cab649d" :answer-field/id #uuid "09bef14a-87dd-54de-aa74-0d9d9cab649d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ed3cec0d-40d3-5e91-911a-bbaee6095b24" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0973e9ca-e0a7-571c-a8f0-019ff57826b5" "answer-5533b44b-f929-586d-b63a-eb6b4676aff7" "answer-cdd35525-6aa6-5770-8013-b818e7e4d6b4" "answer-8b926eb0-063a-5a1d-8cbb-886a18b3afe7" "answer-ed3cec0d-40d3-5e91-911a-bbaee6095b24"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0973e9ca-e0a7-571c-a8f0-019ff57826b5" :answer/id #uuid "0973e9ca-e0a7-571c-a8f0-019ff57826b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5533b44b-f929-586d-b63a-eb6b4676aff7" :answer/id #uuid "5533b44b-f929-586d-b63a-eb6b4676aff7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cdd35525-6aa6-5770-8013-b818e7e4d6b4" :answer/id #uuid "cdd35525-6aa6-5770-8013-b818e7e4d6b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b926eb0-063a-5a1d-8cbb-886a18b3afe7" :answer/id #uuid "8b926eb0-063a-5a1d-8cbb-886a18b3afe7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed3cec0d-40d3-5e91-911a-bbaee6095b24" :answer/id #uuid "ed3cec0d-40d3-5e91-911a-bbaee6095b24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-be1595d6-b16a-5715-995c-d3645afe8a1e" :question/id #uuid "be1595d6-b16a-5715-995c-d3645afe8a1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-64729" :question/problem "Given the ellipse $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{2}=1$, find its intercepts with the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{(0-1)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{1}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{10} & =\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =1 \\\\ y+1 & =\\pm 1 \\\\ y & =-1\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $y=-2$ and $y=0.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,-2,0)$ and $(0,0,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f4183e30-864f-59d2-a111-26fabe8674fe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f4183e30-864f-59d2-a111-26fabe8674fe" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4183e30-864f-59d2-a111-26fabe8674fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-26ab3ac5-f520-5775-ae79-28d69c2b721d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-26ab3ac5-f520-5775-ae79-28d69c2b721d" "answer-322693c6-801e-530e-a07a-0cf0972d13fd" "answer-94022cd2-8c4f-5fd7-b797-94b3f7dfe921" "answer-92f1d345-9338-572b-a022-a2aa7c192bc6" "answer-3b62ac1c-ec02-5ef6-83c0-b9d4f5799d95"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26ab3ac5-f520-5775-ae79-28d69c2b721d" :answer/id #uuid "26ab3ac5-f520-5775-ae79-28d69c2b721d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,-2,0)$ and $(0,0,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-322693c6-801e-530e-a07a-0cf0972d13fd" :answer/id #uuid "322693c6-801e-530e-a07a-0cf0972d13fd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,-\\frac{2}{5},0)$ and $(0,-\\frac{8}{5},0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94022cd2-8c4f-5fd7-b797-94b3f7dfe921" :answer/id #uuid "94022cd2-8c4f-5fd7-b797-94b3f7dfe921" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,2,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92f1d345-9338-572b-a022-a2aa7c192bc6" :answer/id #uuid "92f1d345-9338-572b-a022-a2aa7c192bc6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,\\frac{1}{5},0)$ and $(0,-\\frac{3}{5},0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b62ac1c-ec02-5ef6-83c0-b9d4f5799d95" :answer/id #uuid "3b62ac1c-ec02-5ef6-83c0-b9d4f5799d95" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,\\frac{3}{10},0)$ and $(0,-\\frac{3}{10},0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186378913 :question/worked-solution "To find the $z$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\$\\frac{(0-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(0-1)^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{18} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{18} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{z}^{2}}{18} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =9 \\\\ z & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $z=-3$ and $z=3.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-3)$ and $(0,0,3).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186419596 :question/worked-solution "From the ellipsoid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}+(z-1)^{2} & =1 \\\\ (z-1)^{2} & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4} \\\\ z-1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}\\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the interior of the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}=1$ and its boundary. \n\nTherefore, the domain is \n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}\\le 1\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186419595 :answer-field/correct "answer-0d3c96ea-5670-502d-8704-137e6b80890c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-214587ee-5a72-54a5-bc0e-f7077300d975" "answer-0ab49ac7-5a6c-58cb-87a6-825f1cb8f419" "answer-85156f66-70b0-5f66-992e-d91104d46a3b" "answer-f2240426-8bf1-53c9-881b-8abf1853d3b8" "answer-0d3c96ea-5670-502d-8704-137e6b80890c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-214587ee-5a72-54a5-bc0e-f7077300d975" :answer/id #uuid "214587ee-5a72-54a5-bc0e-f7077300d975" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}>1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ab49ac7-5a6c-58cb-87a6-825f1cb8f419" :answer/id #uuid "0ab49ac7-5a6c-58cb-87a6-825f1cb8f419" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}\\le 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85156f66-70b0-5f66-992e-d91104d46a3b" :answer/id #uuid "85156f66-70b0-5f66-992e-d91104d46a3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}<1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2240426-8bf1-53c9-881b-8abf1853d3b8" :answer/id #uuid "f2240426-8bf1-53c9-881b-8abf1853d3b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}>1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d3c96ea-5670-502d-8704-137e6b80890c" :answer/id #uuid "0d3c96ea-5670-502d-8704-137e6b80890c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}\\le 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284472 :question/worked-solution "From the ellipsoid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}+{y}^{2}+\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{5} & =1 \\\\ (z+1)^{2} & =5(1-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}-{y}^{2}) \\\\ z+1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{5(1-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}-{y}^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}-{y}^{2}\\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}+{y}^{2}\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the interior of the ellipse $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}+{y}^{2}=1$ and its boundary. \n\nTherefore, the domain is \n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}+{y}^{2}\\le 1\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284357 :answer-field/correct "answer-6578a17f-6504-51fd-836a-0aaca0335274" :answer-field/choices ["answer-84934c80-5b5a-533d-bf99-16c473356536" "answer-48abc19a-6b5d-5c36-b5d4-fc5eefeeb76e" "answer-22760f57-3124-5878-9b94-278f7e5b10fb" "answer-a517551e-b8df-5ff5-9c71-4f55e5aaf68a" "answer-6578a17f-6504-51fd-836a-0aaca0335274"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84934c80-5b5a-533d-bf99-16c473356536" :answer/id #uuid "84934c80-5b5a-533d-bf99-16c473356536" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{10}<1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48abc19a-6b5d-5c36-b5d4-fc5eefeeb76e" :answer/id #uuid "48abc19a-6b5d-5c36-b5d4-fc5eefeeb76e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{10}<1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22760f57-3124-5878-9b94-278f7e5b10fb" :answer/id #uuid "22760f57-3124-5878-9b94-278f7e5b10fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{10}<1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a517551e-b8df-5ff5-9c71-4f55e5aaf68a" :answer/id #uuid "a517551e-b8df-5ff5-9c71-4f55e5aaf68a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{10}>1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6578a17f-6504-51fd-836a-0aaca0335274" :answer/id #uuid "6578a17f-6504-51fd-836a-0aaca0335274" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}+{y}^{2}\\le 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b46dd9b0-6a80-5531-9884-f4687e775cb2" :question/id #uuid "b46dd9b0-6a80-5531-9884-f4687e775cb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-70487" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-1)^{2}=2?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the sphere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(0)^{2}+(z-1)^{2}=2 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(z-1)^{2}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-aa0cb4b6-a616-5b8f-b534-fcf340469087"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-aa0cb4b6-a616-5b8f-b534-fcf340469087" :answer-field/id #uuid "aa0cb4b6-a616-5b8f-b534-fcf340469087" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-60315c93-1ed6-5daa-b8f2-20d4ac6ba748" :answer-field/choices ["answer-584822f5-08a3-58ab-b2e2-b93186d19784" "answer-60315c93-1ed6-5daa-b8f2-20d4ac6ba748" "answer-00ddf948-b4f2-5570-a9a2-cfeb90393262" "answer-9424b3f7-d0f0-5bce-803a-28321ac7f675" "answer-214e9af2-9dcc-58c5-a4b5-fda2774bf47b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-584822f5-08a3-58ab-b2e2-b93186d19784" :answer/id #uuid "584822f5-08a3-58ab-b2e2-b93186d19784" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+{z}^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60315c93-1ed6-5daa-b8f2-20d4ac6ba748" :answer/id #uuid "60315c93-1ed6-5daa-b8f2-20d4ac6ba748" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(z-1)^{2}=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00ddf948-b4f2-5570-a9a2-cfeb90393262" :answer/id #uuid "00ddf948-b4f2-5570-a9a2-cfeb90393262" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9424b3f7-d0f0-5bce-803a-28321ac7f675" :answer/id #uuid "9424b3f7-d0f0-5bce-803a-28321ac7f675" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-214e9af2-9dcc-58c5-a4b5-fda2774bf47b" :answer/id #uuid "214e9af2-9dcc-58c5-a4b5-fda2774bf47b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}+(z-1)^{2}=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-15b3432d-8b0c-5d62-a84d-7dadd72f7ac7" :question/id #uuid "15b3432d-8b0c-5d62-a84d-7dadd72f7ac7" :question/math-academy-id "q-73216" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the ellipsoid $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{12}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the ellipsoid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{12}=1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{12}=1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{6})^{2}}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{3})^{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of the ellipse with semi-axes $\\sqrt{6}$ and $2\\sqrt{3},$ centered at $(-1,1)$ in the $yz$-plane." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4dae42d3-3f69-5f16-a665-8518e5d1111c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4dae42d3-3f69-5f16-a665-8518e5d1111c" :answer-field/id #uuid "4dae42d3-3f69-5f16-a665-8518e5d1111c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bc922231-524b-5a1a-85e8-999ef648b749" :answer-field/choices ["answer-003023dc-51c9-58e2-b59b-9f0ea7d84f7d" "answer-f48baf3b-f02e-5d1c-8183-91b15a183361" "answer-1f892faa-9f38-5185-b735-5e66823a7dd8" "answer-bc922231-524b-5a1a-85e8-999ef648b749" "answer-2316a495-6ef9-5785-8b09-333b0185ce24"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-003023dc-51c9-58e2-b59b-9f0ea7d84f7d" :answer/id #uuid "003023dc-51c9-58e2-b59b-9f0ea7d84f7d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An ellipse with semi-axes $6$ and $12,$ centered at $(1,-1)$ in the $yz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f48baf3b-f02e-5d1c-8183-91b15a183361" :answer/id #uuid "f48baf3b-f02e-5d1c-8183-91b15a183361" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An ellipse with semi-axes $6$ and $2\\sqrt{3},$ centered at $(1,-1)$ in the $yz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f892faa-9f38-5185-b735-5e66823a7dd8" :answer/id #uuid "1f892faa-9f38-5185-b735-5e66823a7dd8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An ellipse with semi-axes $\\sqrt{6}$ and $12,$ centered at $(1,1)$ in the $yz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc922231-524b-5a1a-85e8-999ef648b749" :answer/id #uuid "bc922231-524b-5a1a-85e8-999ef648b749" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An ellipse with semi-axes $\\sqrt{6}$ and $2\\sqrt{3},$ centered at $(-1,1)$ in the $yz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2316a495-6ef9-5785-8b09-333b0185ce24" :answer/id #uuid "2316a495-6ef9-5785-8b09-333b0185ce24" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An ellipse with semi-axes $\\sqrt{6}$ and $2\\sqrt{3},$ centered at $(1,-1)$ in the $yz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186159710 :answer-field/choices 17592186159712] [:db/retract 17592186159710 :answer-field/choices 17592186159715] {:db/id 17592186175993 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fe770e3a-7d81-54be-9346-77bf6627bbf9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-fe770e3a-7d81-54be-9346-77bf6627bbf9" :question/id #uuid "fe770e3a-7d81-54be-9346-77bf6627bbf9" :question/math-academy-id "q-109835" :question/problem "Suppose that a matrix $D$ has characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda )=(\\lambda +e)^{4}(\\lambda -\\pi )^{3}(\\lambda -1)^{5},$ the nullity of $(D+eI)^{3}$ equals $3,$ and the nullity of $(D+eI)^{4}$ equals $4.$ If a basis of ${R}^{12}$ consists of linearly independent generalized eigenvectors of $D,$ how many of these are generalized eigenvectors of rank $4$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-e?$" :question/worked-solution "For the given matrix $D$ with eigenvalue $\\lambda =-e,$ a generalized eigenvector of rank $4$ is a vector $v$ such that \n\n$$\n(D+eI)^{4}v=0\\,\\text{and}\\,(D+eI)^{3}v\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nNotice the following:\n\n- We are given that $\\text{Null}(D+eI)^{3}$ has dimension $3.$ This means that the solutions to $(D+eI)^{3}v=0$ form a subspace of dimension $3.$\n\n- We are given that $\\text{Null}(D+eI)^{4}$ has dimension $4.$ This means that the solutions to $(D+eI)^{4}v=0$ form a subspace of dimension $4.$\n\nNow, since $\\text{Null}(D+eI)^{3}$ is a subspace of dimension $2$ in $\\text{Null}(D+eI)^{4}$, which is a subspace of dimension $4,$ our basis can contain only $1$ vector that lies in $\\text{Null}(D+eI)^{4}$ but does not lie in $\\text{Null}(D+eI)^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, there will be \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(D+eI)^{4}-\\text{nullity}(D+eI)^{3}=4-3=1\n$$\n\n generalized eigenvector of rank $4$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-e.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6c1973d3-4cfd-50f8-81d5-f1c3b35c4846"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6c1973d3-4cfd-50f8-81d5-f1c3b35c4846" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c1973d3-4cfd-50f8-81d5-f1c3b35c4846" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-14be5dd6-fd36-5a08-a677-f6f5e4980f1f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-14be5dd6-fd36-5a08-a677-f6f5e4980f1f" "answer-de2afa21-f6ff-5915-a8ab-239729b5c4dd" "answer-5e88b7b2-c4a2-5f46-b0d0-299f26aaf066" "answer-e72807a2-0780-5981-82b2-b6a4a2adee11" "answer-b8ded33d-31c7-56d3-a266-03c82ae475fb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14be5dd6-fd36-5a08-a677-f6f5e4980f1f" :answer/id #uuid "14be5dd6-fd36-5a08-a677-f6f5e4980f1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de2afa21-f6ff-5915-a8ab-239729b5c4dd" :answer/id #uuid "de2afa21-f6ff-5915-a8ab-239729b5c4dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e88b7b2-c4a2-5f46-b0d0-299f26aaf066" :answer/id #uuid "5e88b7b2-c4a2-5f46-b0d0-299f26aaf066" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e72807a2-0780-5981-82b2-b6a4a2adee11" :answer/id #uuid "e72807a2-0780-5981-82b2-b6a4a2adee11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8ded33d-31c7-56d3-a266-03c82ae475fb" :answer/id #uuid "b8ded33d-31c7-56d3-a266-03c82ae475fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162418 :question/problem "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Let the joint CDF of $X$ and $Y$ be $F(x,y),$ where the supports of $X$ and $Y$, respectively, are\n\n$$\n{S}_{X}=\\{1,2,3,4\\},\\,{S}_{Y}=\\{0,1,2,3\\}.\n$$\n\nFind an expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $x>4,y>3.$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables with the joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then the corresponding joint CDF is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)={\\sum }_{{x}_{i}\\le x}{\\sum }_{{y}_{i}\\le y}f({x}_{i},{y}_{i}).\n$$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- We can think of each point where $f(x,y)\\ne 0$ as a point mass in the plane, where the \"probability mass\" at each point equals the probability associated with that point.\n\n- The joint CDF $F(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)$ is the total \"probability mass\" that lies in the infinite rectangular region that has its top-right corner at $(x,y)$ and whose sides are parallel to the coordinate axis.\n\nGiven the supports of $X$ and $Y,$ the joint support $S$ is a subset of\n\n$$\n{S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}=\\{1,2,3,4\\}\\times \\{0,1,2,3\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's sketch the points in ${S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y},$ which contains the joint support. Let's also consider a point $(x,y)$ where $x>4$ and $y>3,$ and a region $Δ$ that lies below and to the left of this point. \n\n![](images/57/575107f600fc73bfa39978f161d9ba9da2ec9315d7be4487e7069ceb4ac590c6.png)\n\nSince every value in the support of $X$ is at most $4$ and $x>4,$ every value in the support of $X$ satisfies $X\\le x.$ Similarly, every value in the support of $Y$ is at most $3$ and $y>3,$ so every possible value of $Y$ satisfies $Y\\le y.$\n\nTherefore, the region $Δ$ contains the entire joint support, and\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186159710 :answer-field/correct 17592186159711 :answer-field/choices ["answer-74d609b3-8497-5d75-9db4-4e0b45bf9758" "answer-3e75a3b1-6dd8-5049-bd03-0ad759293c18"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74d609b3-8497-5d75-9db4-4e0b45bf9758" :answer/id #uuid "74d609b3-8497-5d75-9db4-4e0b45bf9758" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{y}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e75a3b1-6dd8-5049-bd03-0ad759293c18" :answer/id #uuid "3e75a3b1-6dd8-5049-bd03-0ad759293c18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{y}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162003 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a321d767-b173-540f-8a02-df4dc515c060"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a321d767-b173-540f-8a02-df4dc515c060" :question/id #uuid "a321d767-b173-540f-8a02-df4dc515c060" :question/math-academy-id "q-127094" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a random variable with the probability density function shown below. What are the modes of $X?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)+2), & 0\\le x\\le 3 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The modes of a random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ at the global maxima of $f(x).$\n\nTo find the global maxima of $f(x),$ we find the critical points of $f(x)$ and then apply the candidates test.\n\nFirst, we find the critical points.\n\n- The piece of $f(x)$ defined on $0\\le x\\le 3$ is $f(x)=\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)+2).$ Taking the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{6}\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{6}\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)=0\\,⟹\\,\\pi x=0+k\\pi \\,⟹\\,x=k,\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is any integer.\nAmong these critical points, only four lie within the interval $[0,3].$ These are $x=0,1,2,3,$ so we keep them all.\n\n- The derivative doesn't exist at the endpoints $x=0,3.$ So, these are critical points as well, but they are included above.\n\nNow, we evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points $x=0,1,2,3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi (0))+2)=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ f(1) & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi (1))+2)=\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ f(2) & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi (2))+2)=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ f(3) & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi (3))+2)=\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compare all of the values above. The largest values are\n\n$$\nf(0)=f(2)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the modes of $X$ are $0$ and $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c93dfc36-0f20-5d6b-ba00-c7c282eff3ef"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c93dfc36-0f20-5d6b-ba00-c7c282eff3ef" :answer-field/id #uuid "c93dfc36-0f20-5d6b-ba00-c7c282eff3ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-57b32dc3-3595-5c57-8a49-20c39bedb11f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-57b32dc3-3595-5c57-8a49-20c39bedb11f" "answer-25571277-f7a5-5289-a8ba-fe98639976b9" "answer-ba07e6b8-5e9f-5a76-add8-0070f7af1151" "answer-5224e1dd-be47-5d3a-96e7-1006ac12e8af" "answer-d5124caf-6b29-53bb-9a3b-83f8084a1569"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57b32dc3-3595-5c57-8a49-20c39bedb11f" :answer/id #uuid "57b32dc3-3595-5c57-8a49-20c39bedb11f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25571277-f7a5-5289-a8ba-fe98639976b9" :answer/id #uuid "25571277-f7a5-5289-a8ba-fe98639976b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0,2,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba07e6b8-5e9f-5a76-add8-0070f7af1151" :answer/id #uuid "ba07e6b8-5e9f-5a76-add8-0070f7af1151" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5224e1dd-be47-5d3a-96e7-1006ac12e8af" :answer/id #uuid "5224e1dd-be47-5d3a-96e7-1006ac12e8af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5124caf-6b29-53bb-9a3b-83f8084a1569" :answer/id #uuid "d5124caf-6b29-53bb-9a3b-83f8084a1569" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147445 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5b04f6fb-738e-5fda-ac4b-d00fe6581051" "question-4be05fa7-5d88-5239-abf6-50f8cd96f574"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5b04f6fb-738e-5fda-ac4b-d00fe6581051" :question/id #uuid "5b04f6fb-738e-5fda-ac4b-d00fe6581051" :question/math-academy-id "q-94303" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing light damping\n\nII. ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+4y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing critical damping\n\nIII. ${y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+3y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing heavy damping" :question/worked-solution "Remember that, given the equation of a damped harmonic oscillator, the type of damping depends on the discriminant of the characteristic equation:\n\n- $D>0$ leads to heavy damping,\n\n- $D=0$ leads to critical damping, and\n\n- $D<0$ leads to light damping.\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each equation.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+y$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +1=0.\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={4}^{2}-4(1)(1) & =12>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents heavy damping, and so statement I is false.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+4y=0$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +4=0.\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={4}^{2}-4(1)(4) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents critical damping, and so statement II is true.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+3y$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +3=0.\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={3}^{2}-4(1)(3) & =-3<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents light damping, and so statement III is false.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e27cb884-58cc-5969-9740-465e694a1153"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e27cb884-58cc-5969-9740-465e694a1153" :answer-field/id #uuid "e27cb884-58cc-5969-9740-465e694a1153" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6504e2ed-8c9d-555d-8fcf-97583995dc0b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-81118184-833a-5a24-a8a8-080246689d03" "answer-b072fa82-4f42-520f-9a28-4cf9d7117181" "answer-dabc169e-2bef-5859-8318-71f376774cfa" "answer-6504e2ed-8c9d-555d-8fcf-97583995dc0b" "answer-7a00fba0-2dea-5ba8-b58e-77f73a4f66ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81118184-833a-5a24-a8a8-080246689d03" :answer/id #uuid "81118184-833a-5a24-a8a8-080246689d03" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b072fa82-4f42-520f-9a28-4cf9d7117181" :answer/id #uuid "b072fa82-4f42-520f-9a28-4cf9d7117181" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dabc169e-2bef-5859-8318-71f376774cfa" :answer/id #uuid "dabc169e-2bef-5859-8318-71f376774cfa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6504e2ed-8c9d-555d-8fcf-97583995dc0b" :answer/id #uuid "6504e2ed-8c9d-555d-8fcf-97583995dc0b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a00fba0-2dea-5ba8-b58e-77f73a4f66ad" :answer/id #uuid "7a00fba0-2dea-5ba8-b58e-77f73a4f66ad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-00577aba-9963-5deb-b814-1ea4065846a2" :activity/id #uuid "00577aba-9963-5deb-b814-1ea4065846a2" :activity/title "Quiz 6" :activity/type :activity.type/assessment :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-d376774b-1290-557f-84a3-c6190f1e317c" "step-cc01329d-ea2a-5f16-9365-e0876b3fd961" "step-5e9e6af9-ebf7-5415-a0ec-ae18a3d81a55" "step-cb0d7a20-49d9-5f92-88a2-05da28c97dd2" "step-c28639f1-c139-5eb1-b499-5035a6216a8e" "step-9b8993f0-411f-5a90-8d98-e97c774a5798" "step-19ff9675-2577-5ff5-a7b4-7a7e7b5cf512"] :activity/first-step "step-d376774b-1290-557f-84a3-c6190f1e317c" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-d376774b-1290-557f-84a3-c6190f1e317c" :step/id #uuid "d376774b-1290-557f-84a3-c6190f1e317c" :step/content "question-fe770e3a-7d81-54be-9346-77bf6627bbf9" :step/next "step-cc01329d-ea2a-5f16-9365-e0876b3fd961" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-cc01329d-ea2a-5f16-9365-e0876b3fd961" :step/id #uuid "cc01329d-ea2a-5f16-9365-e0876b3fd961" :step/content 17592186435809 :step/next "step-5e9e6af9-ebf7-5415-a0ec-ae18a3d81a55" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-5e9e6af9-ebf7-5415-a0ec-ae18a3d81a55" :step/id #uuid "5e9e6af9-ebf7-5415-a0ec-ae18a3d81a55" :step/content 17592186354309 :step/next "step-cb0d7a20-49d9-5f92-88a2-05da28c97dd2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-cb0d7a20-49d9-5f92-88a2-05da28c97dd2" :step/id #uuid "cb0d7a20-49d9-5f92-88a2-05da28c97dd2" :step/content 17592186162418 :step/next "step-c28639f1-c139-5eb1-b499-5035a6216a8e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c28639f1-c139-5eb1-b499-5035a6216a8e" :step/id #uuid "c28639f1-c139-5eb1-b499-5035a6216a8e" :step/content 17592186559788 :step/next "step-9b8993f0-411f-5a90-8d98-e97c774a5798" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-9b8993f0-411f-5a90-8d98-e97c774a5798" :step/id #uuid "9b8993f0-411f-5a90-8d98-e97c774a5798" :step/content "question-a321d767-b173-540f-8a02-df4dc515c060" :step/next "step-19ff9675-2577-5ff5-a7b4-7a7e7b5cf512" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-19ff9675-2577-5ff5-a7b4-7a7e7b5cf512" :step/id #uuid "19ff9675-2577-5ff5-a7b4-7a7e7b5cf512" :step/content "question-5b04f6fb-738e-5fda-ac4b-d00fe6581051" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204598 :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n2px=3x+5\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $ax=b.$ \n\nWe start by subtracting $3x$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2px & =3x+5 \\\\ 2px-3x & =3x+5-3x \\\\ 2px-3x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $x$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(2p-3)x=5.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $ax=b:$\n\n$$\n{{(2p-3)}_{⏟}}_{a}x={{5}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n2p-3=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2p-3 & =0 \\\\ 2p-3+3 & =0+3 \\\\ 2p & =3 \\\\ \\frac{2p}{2} & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ p & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203497 :answer-field/correct 17592186203502 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "activity-c337d6eb-3aa0-55bd-86e4-7976b5c91d04" :activity/id #uuid "c337d6eb-3aa0-55bd-86e4-7976b5c91d04" :activity/title "Linear Equations With No Solutions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050884 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-1866355e-5a27-511e-8e09-7bbdcb7e2ecf" "step-f4a9ce2d-f2d1-5c3c-aac6-760f7e33d1b4" "step-9195a63d-152b-58e5-95a9-d8c8dcb4ee50"] :activity/first-step "step-1866355e-5a27-511e-8e09-7bbdcb7e2ecf" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-1866355e-5a27-511e-8e09-7bbdcb7e2ecf" :step/id #uuid "1866355e-5a27-511e-8e09-7bbdcb7e2ecf" :step/content 17592186204598 :step/next "step-f4a9ce2d-f2d1-5c3c-aac6-760f7e33d1b4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f4a9ce2d-f2d1-5c3c-aac6-760f7e33d1b4" :step/id #uuid "f4a9ce2d-f2d1-5c3c-aac6-760f7e33d1b4" :step/content 17592186297197 :step/next "step-9195a63d-152b-58e5-95a9-d8c8dcb4ee50" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-9195a63d-152b-58e5-95a9-d8c8dcb4ee50" :step/id #uuid "9195a63d-152b-58e5-95a9-d8c8dcb4ee50" :step/content 17592186297202 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152231 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2ca84db7-67f2-5f23-9873-fa001c3f6805" "question-bfe6201a-0cdf-54aa-a233-33c1bb74e932"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152149 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-38c907cd-2c27-580b-8563-70cc82b39b8b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152148 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-aebb283d-a6dd-5621-b2da-04fb6f0be9f3" "question-559bc70c-78ac-5c05-9067-d915f9f4b231"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2ca84db7-67f2-5f23-9873-fa001c3f6805" :question/id #uuid "2ca84db7-67f2-5f23-9873-fa001c3f6805" :question/math-academy-id "q-122951" :question/problem "![](images/8a/8a418e8e8e84133cb672d312f5dde246876a0f261c97d739b62b7e5ced437764.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the lower Riemann sum $L$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $4$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nL={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{13}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{13}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=\\text{Area}({R}_{13})=1,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={m}_{11}+3\\cdot {m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{13} \\\\  & ={m}_{11}+3{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e5b07574-165a-5003-a2ce-65d9f6400776"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e5b07574-165a-5003-a2ce-65d9f6400776" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5b07574-165a-5003-a2ce-65d9f6400776" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cac5a269-d1ef-595c-a5de-d2913ed48562" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5ce993e2-3ca8-54ad-a607-312b53786484" "answer-aeaf7430-4820-5029-9e60-633211b0422f" "answer-cac5a269-d1ef-595c-a5de-d2913ed48562" "answer-5efcdd19-7c67-5031-a1b4-d680584b5e7b" "answer-7101590f-560d-56a0-92f5-866a481a1aa1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ce993e2-3ca8-54ad-a607-312b53786484" :answer/id #uuid "5ce993e2-3ca8-54ad-a607-312b53786484" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3({m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{13})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aeaf7430-4820-5029-9e60-633211b0422f" :answer/id #uuid "aeaf7430-4820-5029-9e60-633211b0422f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{m}_{11}+3{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cac5a269-d1ef-595c-a5de-d2913ed48562" :answer/id #uuid "cac5a269-d1ef-595c-a5de-d2913ed48562" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{m}_{11}+3{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5efcdd19-7c67-5031-a1b4-d680584b5e7b" :answer/id #uuid "5efcdd19-7c67-5031-a1b4-d680584b5e7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+3{m}_{12}+{m}_{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7101590f-560d-56a0-92f5-866a481a1aa1" :answer/id #uuid "7101590f-560d-56a0-92f5-866a481a1aa1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bfe6201a-0cdf-54aa-a233-33c1bb74e932" :question/id #uuid "bfe6201a-0cdf-54aa-a233-33c1bb74e932" :question/math-academy-id "q-122873" :question/problem "![](images/c6/c6ed4ab6e979f6df3cba0b2afc442dec11667b7b81027cd692e01f1106ee53fa.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the lower Riemann sum $L$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $3$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nL={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31}).\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=\\text{Area}({R}_{31})=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =2\\cdot {m}_{11}+2\\cdot {m}_{21}+2\\cdot {m}_{31} \\\\  & =2({m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{31}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-61541d20-7c76-5499-b8e4-4955bf8e417c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-61541d20-7c76-5499-b8e4-4955bf8e417c" :answer-field/id #uuid "61541d20-7c76-5499-b8e4-4955bf8e417c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4fc140b2-ecc8-5327-bddd-61b81b9f4427" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4fc140b2-ecc8-5327-bddd-61b81b9f4427" "answer-a52d19ad-294e-5ebe-afc8-bb1ccf084e43" "answer-3800ea81-5813-5881-9876-a8523b318270" "answer-f11656ee-b6cc-56d4-b249-32402c686bc5" "answer-faf1dc4d-ba4d-5d53-a2f0-fd3508c89b44"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4fc140b2-ecc8-5327-bddd-61b81b9f4427" :answer/id #uuid "4fc140b2-ecc8-5327-bddd-61b81b9f4427" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{31})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a52d19ad-294e-5ebe-afc8-bb1ccf084e43" :answer/id #uuid "a52d19ad-294e-5ebe-afc8-bb1ccf084e43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{31}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3800ea81-5813-5881-9876-a8523b318270" :answer/id #uuid "3800ea81-5813-5881-9876-a8523b318270" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{m}_{11}-{m}_{21}-{m}_{31}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f11656ee-b6cc-56d4-b249-32402c686bc5" :answer/id #uuid "f11656ee-b6cc-56d4-b249-32402c686bc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{31}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-faf1dc4d-ba4d-5d53-a2f0-fd3508c89b44" :answer/id #uuid "faf1dc4d-ba4d-5d53-a2f0-fd3508c89b44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{m}_{11}\\cdot {m}_{21}\\cdot {m}_{31}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-38c907cd-2c27-580b-8563-70cc82b39b8b" :question/id #uuid "38c907cd-2c27-580b-8563-70cc82b39b8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-75038" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=4-x-y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{0,1,2\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{0,1,2\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/3c/3cac974f7352243bfbe008ad8af58ae8222709f81f434070383cc759a46747c7.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=4-x-y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=4-x-y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/0f/0fefe892c74e8d391e56ee822f83e7e0fe0110593c9d6a4b93b8cfe1e558ab16.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/fe/fe872f1f1b0307760dcdba6ac6f6be20f197662ac250ab46dc77fa472295906f.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,1)=2 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,1)=1 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(1,2)=1 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(2,2)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=2+1+1+0=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b76b9c41-1ad3-5f84-b769-5d10b8aa414c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b76b9c41-1ad3-5f84-b769-5d10b8aa414c" :answer-field/id #uuid "b76b9c41-1ad3-5f84-b769-5d10b8aa414c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-996732db-d52d-5214-965f-c7db143a083d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-69c6207d-8d80-5cde-8944-57ceb4aef0c3" "answer-996732db-d52d-5214-965f-c7db143a083d" "answer-8c966508-5722-5ab1-b2e6-984f8b68946d" "answer-57479917-67d8-5013-96bf-d03d0cec796d" "answer-d83a61cf-5027-53d7-a7f2-fe2053a5b5de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69c6207d-8d80-5cde-8944-57ceb4aef0c3" :answer/id #uuid "69c6207d-8d80-5cde-8944-57ceb4aef0c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-996732db-d52d-5214-965f-c7db143a083d" :answer/id #uuid "996732db-d52d-5214-965f-c7db143a083d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c966508-5722-5ab1-b2e6-984f8b68946d" :answer/id #uuid "8c966508-5722-5ab1-b2e6-984f8b68946d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57479917-67d8-5013-96bf-d03d0cec796d" :answer/id #uuid "57479917-67d8-5013-96bf-d03d0cec796d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d83a61cf-5027-53d7-a7f2-fe2053a5b5de" :answer/id #uuid "d83a61cf-5027-53d7-a7f2-fe2053a5b5de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-aebb283d-a6dd-5621-b2da-04fb6f0be9f3" :question/id #uuid "aebb283d-a6dd-5621-b2da-04fb6f0be9f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-75231" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,1]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=3x+y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{0,1\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/c2/c2c33fe367e36506f949f1f76d84ccb2b3ff74ea3a4456e57982f489978225b3.png)\n\nThe lower sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $2$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{12}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=3x+y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=3x+y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/3b/3bdc77445e75c7c74d6e242f9eb469687aa34384e7399b05607dfaa4a81ae596.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/ac/acded82358333752ba407673edf543262ee0b36166014c3de54d9beef9218a26.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(0,1)=1 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(0,2)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & =1+2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4f9c92a2-2c2c-5f88-a31b-706d15e85fb5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4f9c92a2-2c2c-5f88-a31b-706d15e85fb5" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f9c92a2-2c2c-5f88-a31b-706d15e85fb5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ea56ea57-0f71-519e-a988-f5b5c4c2111a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ea56ea57-0f71-519e-a988-f5b5c4c2111a" "answer-e4ee0dad-3131-5b08-b7fc-b7b8b68f9a9f" "answer-1b377a21-5851-5233-ba67-1bd25d4c8f74" "answer-9c26311a-5f11-56c5-ade9-4c523fc7c350" "answer-0432d4eb-63b0-56eb-bf7b-7e0a2409ea51"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea56ea57-0f71-519e-a988-f5b5c4c2111a" :answer/id #uuid "ea56ea57-0f71-519e-a988-f5b5c4c2111a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4ee0dad-3131-5b08-b7fc-b7b8b68f9a9f" :answer/id #uuid "e4ee0dad-3131-5b08-b7fc-b7b8b68f9a9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b377a21-5851-5233-ba67-1bd25d4c8f74" :answer/id #uuid "1b377a21-5851-5233-ba67-1bd25d4c8f74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c26311a-5f11-56c5-ade9-4c523fc7c350" :answer/id #uuid "9c26311a-5f11-56c5-ade9-4c523fc7c350" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0432d4eb-63b0-56eb-bf7b-7e0a2409ea51" :answer/id #uuid "0432d4eb-63b0-56eb-bf7b-7e0a2409ea51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152397 :question/problem "Let $R=[0,4]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=2x+3y+1.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{0,2,4\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{0,1,2\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/ff/ff5612495e4f64e710963ca4d4fc6b7b259164c7ef1943aa37467a71c1d48353.png)\n\nThe lower sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=2$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=2{m}_{11}+2{m}_{12}+2{m}_{21}+2{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=2x+3y+1$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=2x+3y+1$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ff/ffa7288d56b6604cf0ad013941003642209cf8ae75eca22d791cc5b65df4de35.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/be/be946433e503c6d7125fd53de795b5606666f20f3aa6164dd7e7b947b08af6d6.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(0,0)=1 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(2,0)=5 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(0,1)=4 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(2,1)=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & =2\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186148913 :answer-field/correct 17592186148918 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-559bc70c-78ac-5c05-9067-d915f9f4b231" :question/id #uuid "559bc70c-78ac-5c05-9067-d915f9f4b231" :question/math-academy-id "q-75235" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,4]\\times [0,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+y+1.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{0,2,4\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{0,2,4\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/29/293e79685a3f4da205d986bcf4331e4b4f43c0a48fe183d27f93aaee6bb17b99.png)\n\nThe lower sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=4$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=4{m}_{11}+4{m}_{21}+4{m}_{12}+4{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+y+1$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+y+1$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/12/12df172e3a2f60a8b123937600d5774508ac8cb204696414690490be8d9e2c32.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/b5/b5e72e970d512740cc0d5de9e2d5739d71fb0c90e750c9874042ff4fa5230db9.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(0,0)=1 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,0)=3 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(0,2)=3 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(2,2)=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & =4\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-352dbe2b-1ccb-5161-9599-03540de2d249"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-352dbe2b-1ccb-5161-9599-03540de2d249" :answer-field/id #uuid "352dbe2b-1ccb-5161-9599-03540de2d249" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-abbcdeef-5cb8-52d6-b2e7-3318843356b0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0f3951a8-dde7-5b56-bc08-28b7fbe0bd99" "answer-ba710b16-4bd3-5083-a30b-2dbd0e05b4a9" "answer-887d8243-ec17-5a15-b60c-9d35f62cb56c" "answer-abbcdeef-5cb8-52d6-b2e7-3318843356b0" "answer-c7084f82-22f4-55a8-a979-f37698ccd1ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f3951a8-dde7-5b56-bc08-28b7fbe0bd99" :answer/id #uuid "0f3951a8-dde7-5b56-bc08-28b7fbe0bd99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba710b16-4bd3-5083-a30b-2dbd0e05b4a9" :answer/id #uuid "ba710b16-4bd3-5083-a30b-2dbd0e05b4a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-887d8243-ec17-5a15-b60c-9d35f62cb56c" :answer/id #uuid "887d8243-ec17-5a15-b60c-9d35f62cb56c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "44" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abbcdeef-5cb8-52d6-b2e7-3318843356b0" :answer/id #uuid "abbcdeef-5cb8-52d6-b2e7-3318843356b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7084f82-22f4-55a8-a979-f37698ccd1ba" :answer/id #uuid "c7084f82-22f4-55a8-a979-f37698ccd1ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "56" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147462 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f97bc019-bf9e-5a95-8fff-fb6e975b8716" "question-d3bc0664-ca47-5557-b277-90c0fa7c4b0b" "question-efae9349-6eb8-5183-b15e-8510c6f912ab"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f97bc019-bf9e-5a95-8fff-fb6e975b8716" :question/id #uuid "f97bc019-bf9e-5a95-8fff-fb6e975b8716" :question/math-academy-id "q-64028" :question/problem "Find the common ratio of the geometric sequence whose fourth term is $8$ and whose seventh term is $216.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the common ratio $r$ of a geometric sequence given two terms ${a}_{m}$ and ${a}_{n},$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n{r}^{n-m}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're given ${a}_{7}=216$ and ${a}_{4}=8.$ Substituting $n=7$ and $m=4$ into the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{7-4} & =\\frac{{a}_{7}}{{a}_{4}} \\\\ {r}^{3} & =\\frac{216}{8} \\\\ {r}^{3} & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by solving the equation for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{3} & =27 \\\\ {r}^{3} & ={3}^{3} \\\\ r & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ef08cdfa-d03c-5a27-9c04-3a7bd62647af"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ef08cdfa-d03c-5a27-9c04-3a7bd62647af" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef08cdfa-d03c-5a27-9c04-3a7bd62647af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7236f903-d1df-5216-92d2-77e4d79341ce" :answer-field/choices ["answer-18ea77fd-c466-5c19-8b78-e55b99ea7fbd" "answer-31a77208-9897-5980-990c-d8cb0c4f2dc2" "answer-7236f903-d1df-5216-92d2-77e4d79341ce" "answer-7f835048-d27c-5354-a28a-6a4708cc3972" "answer-d32eb0f8-d90b-5fd2-b720-1d025deb37b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18ea77fd-c466-5c19-8b78-e55b99ea7fbd" :answer/id #uuid "18ea77fd-c466-5c19-8b78-e55b99ea7fbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31a77208-9897-5980-990c-d8cb0c4f2dc2" :answer/id #uuid "31a77208-9897-5980-990c-d8cb0c4f2dc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7236f903-d1df-5216-92d2-77e4d79341ce" :answer/id #uuid "7236f903-d1df-5216-92d2-77e4d79341ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f835048-d27c-5354-a28a-6a4708cc3972" :answer/id #uuid "7f835048-d27c-5354-a28a-6a4708cc3972" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d32eb0f8-d90b-5fd2-b720-1d025deb37b1" :answer/id #uuid "d32eb0f8-d90b-5fd2-b720-1d025deb37b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d3bc0664-ca47-5557-b277-90c0fa7c4b0b" :question/id #uuid "d3bc0664-ca47-5557-b277-90c0fa7c4b0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-250933" :question/problem "Find the common ratio of the geometric sequence whose fifth term is $7$ and whose tenth term is $-224.$\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the common ratio $r$ of a geometric sequence given two terms ${a}_{m}$ and ${a}_{n},$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n{r}^{n-m}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're given ${a}_{10}=-224$ and ${a}_{5}=7.$ Substituting $n=10$ and $m=5$ into the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{10-5} & =\\frac{{a}_{10}}{{a}_{5}} \\\\ {r}^{5} & =\\frac{(-224)}{7} \\\\ {r}^{5} & =-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by solving the equation for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{5} & =-32 \\\\ {r}^{5} & =(-2)^{5} \\\\ r & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a19bdd09-342c-5cf6-98d6-201c1aaf72dc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a19bdd09-342c-5cf6-98d6-201c1aaf72dc" :answer-field/id #uuid "a19bdd09-342c-5cf6-98d6-201c1aaf72dc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9ed3028e-ba87-52ad-ae62-bf4a8940254b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9ed3028e-ba87-52ad-ae62-bf4a8940254b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ed3028e-ba87-52ad-ae62-bf4a8940254b" :answer/id #uuid "9ed3028e-ba87-52ad-ae62-bf4a8940254b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-efae9349-6eb8-5183-b15e-8510c6f912ab" :question/id #uuid "efae9349-6eb8-5183-b15e-8510c6f912ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-250939" :question/problem "Find the common ratio of the geometric sequence whose sixth term is $-15$ and whose ninth term is $-\\frac{3}{25}.$\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the common ratio $r$ of a geometric sequence given two terms ${a}_{m}$ and ${a}_{n},$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n{r}^{n-m}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're given ${a}_{9}=-\\frac{3}{25}$ and ${a}_{6}=-15.$ Substituting $n=9$ and $m=6$ into the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{9-6} & =\\frac{{a}_{9}}{{a}_{6}} \\\\ {r}^{3} & =\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{25})}{(-15)} \\\\ {r}^{3} & =\\frac{1}{125}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by solving the equation for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{3} & =\\frac{1}{125} \\\\ {r}^{3} & ={(\\frac{1}{5})}^{3} \\\\ r & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-48a7ef4a-dd0b-5d40-ac05-a0608f5b503d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-48a7ef4a-dd0b-5d40-ac05-a0608f5b503d" :answer-field/id #uuid "48a7ef4a-dd0b-5d40-ac05-a0608f5b503d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8674d049-595e-5d07-a71e-5822b43b9d36" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8674d049-595e-5d07-a71e-5822b43b9d36"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8674d049-595e-5d07-a71e-5822b43b9d36" :answer/id #uuid "8674d049-595e-5d07-a71e-5822b43b9d36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-a066ff8d-e25c-5320-8120-164f3570065b" :activity/id #uuid "a066ff8d-e25c-5320-8120-164f3570065b" :activity/title "Finding the Common Ratio of a Geometric Sequence Given Two Terms" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049083 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-1b47d971-0728-5dcd-be3c-7a4a0a60c7ae" "step-50fb3ac3-f3cc-50d4-9b06-d76aabe80037" "step-1e550813-b681-51bf-a08c-df578a80df5c"] :activity/first-step "step-1b47d971-0728-5dcd-be3c-7a4a0a60c7ae" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-1b47d971-0728-5dcd-be3c-7a4a0a60c7ae" :step/id #uuid "1b47d971-0728-5dcd-be3c-7a4a0a60c7ae" :step/content "question-f97bc019-bf9e-5a95-8fff-fb6e975b8716" :step/next "step-50fb3ac3-f3cc-50d4-9b06-d76aabe80037" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-50fb3ac3-f3cc-50d4-9b06-d76aabe80037" :step/id #uuid "50fb3ac3-f3cc-50d4-9b06-d76aabe80037" :step/content "question-d3bc0664-ca47-5557-b277-90c0fa7c4b0b" :step/next "step-1e550813-b681-51bf-a08c-df578a80df5c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1e550813-b681-51bf-a08c-df578a80df5c" :step/id #uuid "1e550813-b681-51bf-a08c-df578a80df5c" :step/content "question-efae9349-6eb8-5183-b15e-8510c6f912ab" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "question-4be05fa7-5d88-5239-abf6-50f8cd96f574" :question/id #uuid "4be05fa7-5d88-5239-abf6-50f8cd96f574" :question/math-academy-id "q-79501" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+7y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing light damping.\n\nII. ${y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+3y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing critical damping.\n\nIII. ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+12y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing heavy damping." :question/worked-solution "Remember that, given the equation of a damped harmonic oscillator, the type of damping depends on the discriminant of the characteristic equation:\n\n- $D>0$ leads to heavy damping,\n\n- $D=0$ leads to critical damping, and\n\n- $D<0$ leads to light damping.\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each equation.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+7y=0$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +7=0\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={3}^{2}-4(1)(7) & =-19<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents light damping, and so statement I is correct.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+3y=0$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +3=0\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={6}^{2}-4(1)(3) & =24>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents heavy damping, and so statement II is false.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+12y=0$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +12=0.\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={4}^{2}-4(1)(12) & =-32<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents light damping, and so statement III is false.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-127665a7-bfc2-524d-a3d5-c84c27346085"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-127665a7-bfc2-524d-a3d5-c84c27346085" :answer-field/id #uuid "127665a7-bfc2-524d-a3d5-c84c27346085" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f6590b43-8596-5be6-bc68-9a3582197ad7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f7d207a9-c89e-548b-9f38-b94e8ddd223f" "answer-f6590b43-8596-5be6-bc68-9a3582197ad7" "answer-3ed39c37-4e3c-50bf-85ad-851a0f5c1fe8" "answer-5d6ab486-85e0-5bdd-a914-3a2eb53a0b0e" "answer-d55e1983-523e-5bc6-a345-3a7a2d7950ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7d207a9-c89e-548b-9f38-b94e8ddd223f" :answer/id #uuid "f7d207a9-c89e-548b-9f38-b94e8ddd223f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6590b43-8596-5be6-bc68-9a3582197ad7" :answer/id #uuid "f6590b43-8596-5be6-bc68-9a3582197ad7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ed39c37-4e3c-50bf-85ad-851a0f5c1fe8" :answer/id #uuid "3ed39c37-4e3c-50bf-85ad-851a0f5c1fe8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d6ab486-85e0-5bdd-a914-3a2eb53a0b0e" :answer/id #uuid "5d6ab486-85e0-5bdd-a914-3a2eb53a0b0e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d55e1983-523e-5bc6-a345-3a7a2d7950ba" :answer/id #uuid "d55e1983-523e-5bc6-a345-3a7a2d7950ba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147446 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-56b1314a-ceaf-5db3-a203-e533e79bae7a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-56b1314a-ceaf-5db3-a203-e533e79bae7a" :question/id #uuid "56b1314a-ceaf-5db3-a203-e533e79bae7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-94322" :question/problem "A particle of mass $4\\,\\text{kg}$ is attached to a massless spring. The spring constant associated with the spring is $k=4\\,{\\text{kg/s}}^{2}.$  The particle is also subject to a resistive force that's proportional to the particle's velocity, and has a damping coefficient $c=2\\,\\text{kg/s}.$  The position of the particle is $y(t)$ (measured in meters), and $t>0$ is the time in seconds.  If the particle moves with damped harmonic motion, what is the governing equation?" :question/worked-solution "The equation of damped harmonic motion is\n\n$$\nm{y}^{″}=-c{y}^{′}-ky.\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $m,$ $k$ and $c$ gives\n\n$$\n4{y}^{″}=-2{y}^{′}-4y.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{′}+y=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-41f2e569-8706-5300-b37e-a72c9b91421e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-41f2e569-8706-5300-b37e-a72c9b91421e" :answer-field/id #uuid "41f2e569-8706-5300-b37e-a72c9b91421e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6b61a7ea-dcb2-546d-9bdf-b3c1217dba3a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d5da7789-f128-5d0d-9c57-cb303ce4e6e9" "answer-d4eec167-2a30-5587-9ff2-9ff119e2f727" "answer-6b61a7ea-dcb2-546d-9bdf-b3c1217dba3a" "answer-5b2ee954-a441-5a13-b989-1132dca26282" "answer-3b62aaa4-07cf-5e1f-9d53-d1d21bd1d7ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5da7789-f128-5d0d-9c57-cb303ce4e6e9" :answer/id #uuid "d5da7789-f128-5d0d-9c57-cb303ce4e6e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4eec167-2a30-5587-9ff2-9ff119e2f727" :answer/id #uuid "d4eec167-2a30-5587-9ff2-9ff119e2f727" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{′}+2y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b61a7ea-dcb2-546d-9bdf-b3c1217dba3a" :answer/id #uuid "6b61a7ea-dcb2-546d-9bdf-b3c1217dba3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{′}+y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b2ee954-a441-5a13-b989-1132dca26282" :answer/id #uuid "5b2ee954-a441-5a13-b989-1132dca26282" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+2y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b62aaa4-07cf-5e1f-9d53-d1d21bd1d7ab" :answer/id #uuid "3b62aaa4-07cf-5e1f-9d53-d1d21bd1d7ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{2}y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-7aac9d9a-80dd-50d1-aa8b-32026d2b7b98" :activity/id #uuid "7aac9d9a-80dd-50d1-aa8b-32026d2b7b98" :activity/title "Damped Oscillators" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048291 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-99ee008c-724b-5795-b199-dd045f6be029" "step-32206203-4ed0-5734-9397-48990a5beafb" "step-772a7d55-73b7-505c-b338-1e17c49bf086" "step-ce9b1e3d-07cc-56da-b3a1-2106d7f4b4f0" "step-1a0b64b5-8ad7-595a-ad6a-e5e032ce3417"] :activity/first-step "step-99ee008c-724b-5795-b199-dd045f6be029" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-99ee008c-724b-5795-b199-dd045f6be029" :step/id #uuid "99ee008c-724b-5795-b199-dd045f6be029" :step/content "question-4be05fa7-5d88-5239-abf6-50f8cd96f574" :step/next "step-32206203-4ed0-5734-9397-48990a5beafb" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-32206203-4ed0-5734-9397-48990a5beafb" :step/id #uuid "32206203-4ed0-5734-9397-48990a5beafb" :step/content 17592186348240 :step/next "step-772a7d55-73b7-505c-b338-1e17c49bf086" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-772a7d55-73b7-505c-b338-1e17c49bf086" :step/id #uuid "772a7d55-73b7-505c-b338-1e17c49bf086" :step/content 17592186357720 :step/next "step-ce9b1e3d-07cc-56da-b3a1-2106d7f4b4f0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-ce9b1e3d-07cc-56da-b3a1-2106d7f4b4f0" :step/id #uuid "ce9b1e3d-07cc-56da-b3a1-2106d7f4b4f0" :step/content "question-56b1314a-ceaf-5db3-a203-e533e79bae7a" :step/next "step-1a0b64b5-8ad7-595a-ad6a-e5e032ce3417" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1a0b64b5-8ad7-595a-ad6a-e5e032ce3417" :step/id #uuid "1a0b64b5-8ad7-595a-ad6a-e5e032ce3417" :step/content 17592186357733 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054642 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9036632e-a4e5-591e-b6d4-bd5830e984df"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055037 :question/problem "$2$ is prime, **or** $14$ is a multiple of $7$ **and** $5.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $R:2\\text{ is prime}$\n\n- $S:14\\text{ is a multiple of }7$\n\n- $T:14\\text{ is a multiple of }5$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $2$ is prime. This corresponds to $R.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $14$ is a multiple of $7$ and $5.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{14\\text{ is a multiple of }7}_{⏟}}_{S}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{14\\text{ is a multiple of }5}_{⏟}}_{T},\n$$\n\nthat is, $S∧T.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{2\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{R}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{14\\text{ is a multiple of }7\\text{ and }5}_{⏟}}_{S\\,∧\\,T},\n$$\n\nthat is, $R∨(S∧T).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186051752 :answer-field/correct 17592186051754 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-9036632e-a4e5-591e-b6d4-bd5830e984df" :question/id #uuid "9036632e-a4e5-591e-b6d4-bd5830e984df" :question/math-academy-id "q-177452" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{5}$ is rational, **or** $3|12$ **and** $3|18.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P:\\sqrt{5}\\text{ is rational}$\n\n- $Q:3|12$\n\n- $R:3|18\\text{ }$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $\\sqrt{5}$ is rational. This corresponds to $P.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $3|12$ and $3|18.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{3|12}_{⏟}}_{Q}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{3|18}_{⏟}}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $Q∧R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{\\sqrt{5}\\text{ is rational}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{3|12\\text{ and }3|18}_{⏟}}_{Q\\,∧\\,R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∨(Q∧R).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d2accb16-6316-5d25-b406-7af92337b373"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d2accb16-6316-5d25-b406-7af92337b373" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2accb16-6316-5d25-b406-7af92337b373" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-577b7d65-cc3e-5730-82a1-86c384479356" :answer-field/choices ["answer-40a41c4a-74f2-5a0d-80b4-6255b626fcc4" "answer-b1ad3c78-1256-5dff-9d91-4d2324618c7d" "answer-f27b8716-005f-5b70-a4d1-fcf5671b7cd9" "answer-12e69b24-bdab-519d-9db4-fa9f763bec4a" "answer-577b7d65-cc3e-5730-82a1-86c384479356"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40a41c4a-74f2-5a0d-80b4-6255b626fcc4" :answer/id #uuid "40a41c4a-74f2-5a0d-80b4-6255b626fcc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(P∧Q)∨R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1ad3c78-1256-5dff-9d91-4d2324618c7d" :answer/id #uuid "b1ad3c78-1256-5dff-9d91-4d2324618c7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(P∨Q)∧R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f27b8716-005f-5b70-a4d1-fcf5671b7cd9" :answer/id #uuid "f27b8716-005f-5b70-a4d1-fcf5671b7cd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P∧(Q∧R)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12e69b24-bdab-519d-9db4-fa9f763bec4a" :answer/id #uuid "12e69b24-bdab-519d-9db4-fa9f763bec4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P∧(Q∨R)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-577b7d65-cc3e-5730-82a1-86c384479356" :answer/id #uuid "577b7d65-cc3e-5730-82a1-86c384479356" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P∨(Q∧R)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054644 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b08d6228-4d71-56ec-903b-067eaa383489"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b08d6228-4d71-56ec-903b-067eaa383489" :question/id #uuid "b08d6228-4d71-56ec-903b-067eaa383489" :question/math-academy-id "q-178163" :question/problem "$$\n{{0\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{\\{1,2\\}\\cap \\{1\\}=\\{1,2\\}}}\\,\\overset{∨}{\\overset{⏞}{\\text{or}}}\\,\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{2}{3}\\text{ is irrational}}}}_{⏟}}_{Q\\,∨\\,R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $Q∨R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $P∨(Q∨R)$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is true, $Q$ is false, and $R$ is false. Therefore, $Q∨R$ is false, but the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∨(Q∨R) & ≡\\text{true}∨\\overset{\\text{false}}{\\overset{⏞}{(\\text{false}∨\\text{false})}} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}∨\\text{false} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c48b5f22-688c-554b-b977-496452316b1e" "answer-field-9d6f16fd-3b2c-5aaa-8d4b-bff5822eb1f4" "answer-field-1de9cdf1-94b6-56c2-bf7d-3647210da7b1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c48b5f22-688c-554b-b977-496452316b1e" :answer-field/id #uuid "c48b5f22-688c-554b-b977-496452316b1e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-f6d52984-4570-5e61-afbd-0073a1b7199b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cde20091-5ea0-5e89-8e56-3c6da49f96e9" "answer-f6d52984-4570-5e61-afbd-0073a1b7199b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cde20091-5ea0-5e89-8e56-3c6da49f96e9" :answer/id #uuid "cde20091-5ea0-5e89-8e56-3c6da49f96e9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "false" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6d52984-4570-5e61-afbd-0073a1b7199b" :answer/id #uuid "f6d52984-4570-5e61-afbd-0073a1b7199b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9d6f16fd-3b2c-5aaa-8d4b-bff5822eb1f4" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d6f16fd-3b2c-5aaa-8d4b-bff5822eb1f4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-0c62bc40-0349-5024-a000-9e42299ef3ba" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0c62bc40-0349-5024-a000-9e42299ef3ba" "answer-addf42f9-b92a-50aa-840e-9cebd676a066"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c62bc40-0349-5024-a000-9e42299ef3ba" :answer/id #uuid "0c62bc40-0349-5024-a000-9e42299ef3ba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "false" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-addf42f9-b92a-50aa-840e-9cebd676a066" :answer/id #uuid "addf42f9-b92a-50aa-840e-9cebd676a066" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1de9cdf1-94b6-56c2-bf7d-3647210da7b1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1de9cdf1-94b6-56c2-bf7d-3647210da7b1" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-4290994a-4111-5f59-8d28-488485afe845" :answer-field/choices ["answer-56b8008e-3e0e-50d5-b98d-6f1ae9548a59" "answer-4290994a-4111-5f59-8d28-488485afe845"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56b8008e-3e0e-50d5-b98d-6f1ae9548a59" :answer/id #uuid "56b8008e-3e0e-50d5-b98d-6f1ae9548a59" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "false" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4290994a-4111-5f59-8d28-488485afe845" :answer/id #uuid "4290994a-4111-5f59-8d28-488485afe845" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186055087 :question/problem "$$\n{{2\\text{ is negative}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{0.5\\text{ is rational}}_{⏟}}_{B}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $A$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $B$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $A∨B$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is false, and $B$ is true. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{2\\text{ is negative}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{0.5\\text{ is rational}}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{false}∨\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186051971 :answer-field/correct 17592186051973 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186051968 :answer-field/correct 17592186051969 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186051965 :answer-field/correct 17592186051967 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "activity-71a8b3cb-fa15-5adb-be3d-13c0443f9e35" :activity/id #uuid "71a8b3cb-fa15-5adb-be3d-13c0443f9e35" :activity/title "The \"And\" and \"Or\" Connectives" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048778 :activity/course 17592186046668 :activity/steps ["step-8cb69003-9c5b-5348-b98b-bc7093eea6f5" "step-e564f1c7-8cb6-50b6-a505-2ce605981f41" "step-0273e10d-6704-5bf2-969f-e05c1abc5298" "step-7e1dd0ca-0641-5269-abe6-68b013d844af" "step-e5df0196-87e7-5d2d-a973-8fd272f8b83b"] :activity/first-step "step-8cb69003-9c5b-5348-b98b-bc7093eea6f5" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-8cb69003-9c5b-5348-b98b-bc7093eea6f5" :step/id #uuid "8cb69003-9c5b-5348-b98b-bc7093eea6f5" :step/content 17592186055037 :step/next "step-e564f1c7-8cb6-50b6-a505-2ce605981f41" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e564f1c7-8cb6-50b6-a505-2ce605981f41" :step/id #uuid "e564f1c7-8cb6-50b6-a505-2ce605981f41" :step/content 17592186379005 :step/next "step-0273e10d-6704-5bf2-969f-e05c1abc5298" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0273e10d-6704-5bf2-969f-e05c1abc5298" :step/id #uuid "0273e10d-6704-5bf2-969f-e05c1abc5298" :step/content "question-9036632e-a4e5-591e-b6d4-bd5830e984df" :step/next "step-7e1dd0ca-0641-5269-abe6-68b013d844af" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-7e1dd0ca-0641-5269-abe6-68b013d844af" :step/id #uuid "7e1dd0ca-0641-5269-abe6-68b013d844af" :step/content "question-b08d6228-4d71-56ec-903b-067eaa383489" :step/next "step-e5df0196-87e7-5d2d-a973-8fd272f8b83b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e5df0196-87e7-5d2d-a973-8fd272f8b83b" :step/id #uuid "e5df0196-87e7-5d2d-a973-8fd272f8b83b" :step/content 17592186055087 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105741 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b85bf70e-60cf-531c-93a8-54cd5e2b47c0" "question-ae1938a1-58ee-571b-a544-d365ce409563"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b85bf70e-60cf-531c-93a8-54cd5e2b47c0" :question/id #uuid "b85bf70e-60cf-531c-93a8-54cd5e2b47c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-21222" :question/problem "![](images/c6/c62f51c2b029d6b1e24e7f30603c5f34ab5d70d96ed84c5c74de15d4e2e6358e.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of $∠D?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $△ABC$ is an equilateral triangle. Consequently, all of the interior angles must be equal to ${60}^{∘}:$ \n\n$$\nm∠A=m∠B=m∠ABC={60}^{∘}\n$$\n\nAlso, since $△CDB$ is an isosceles triangle, the base angles must have equal measure:\n\n$$\nm∠CBD=m∠D\n$$\n\nNotice also that $∠ACB$ and $∠DCB$ are supplementary, therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠ACB+m∠DCB & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {60}^{∘}+m∠DCB & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠DCB & ={120}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Finally, we calculate $m∠D$ using the fact that the interior angles of a triangle sum to ${180}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠D+m∠DCB+m∠CBD & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠D+{120}^{∘}+m∠D & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2m∠D & ={60}^{∘} \\\\ m∠D & ={30}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a9b88805-312e-50ff-a48f-9a2d91e7b91d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a9b88805-312e-50ff-a48f-9a2d91e7b91d" :answer-field/id #uuid "a9b88805-312e-50ff-a48f-9a2d91e7b91d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a51bdf43-9f1b-54de-9f2e-2698aa8af185" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8be640ca-b6bd-59dc-98b9-bc210f8e3e6a" "answer-7f5c018b-da77-51b3-94a3-4a719e2c22a2" "answer-a51bdf43-9f1b-54de-9f2e-2698aa8af185" "answer-7af2094e-5a9c-5576-ab4c-588a0176acd0" "answer-b7b5d134-db45-5c5c-a672-02898c3558d0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8be640ca-b6bd-59dc-98b9-bc210f8e3e6a" :answer/id #uuid "8be640ca-b6bd-59dc-98b9-bc210f8e3e6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{27}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f5c018b-da77-51b3-94a3-4a719e2c22a2" :answer/id #uuid "7f5c018b-da77-51b3-94a3-4a719e2c22a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{29}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a51bdf43-9f1b-54de-9f2e-2698aa8af185" :answer/id #uuid "a51bdf43-9f1b-54de-9f2e-2698aa8af185" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7af2094e-5a9c-5576-ab4c-588a0176acd0" :answer/id #uuid "7af2094e-5a9c-5576-ab4c-588a0176acd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{32}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7b5d134-db45-5c5c-a672-02898c3558d0" :answer/id #uuid "b7b5d134-db45-5c5c-a672-02898c3558d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{34}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ae1938a1-58ee-571b-a544-d365ce409563" :question/id #uuid "ae1938a1-58ee-571b-a544-d365ce409563" :question/math-academy-id "q-21232" :question/problem "![](images/19/19ca38571817d9de8c92de17d5121c33ac1494848766033792dc9586c95fa475.png)\n\nIn the isosceles triangle $△ABC$  with base $\\overset{―}{AB}$, point $E$ lies on the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$, $\\overset{―}{AE}=\\overset{―}{EC}$ and $m∠EAC={40}^{∘}.$ What is the measure of $∠B?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $△ABC$ is an isosceles triangle with base $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Consequently,  the base angles must have equal measure:\n\n$$\nm∠BAC=m∠B\n$$\n\nAlso, since $△CEA$ is an isosceles triangle, we have:\n\n$$\nm∠C=m∠EAC={40}^{∘}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate $m∠B$ using the fact that the interior angles of $△ABC$ sum to ${180}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠BAC+m∠B+m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B+m∠B+{40}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2m∠B & ={140}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B & ={70}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ddd44795-8d4c-547b-9853-d23d19571f47"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ddd44795-8d4c-547b-9853-d23d19571f47" :answer-field/id #uuid "ddd44795-8d4c-547b-9853-d23d19571f47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-aa458a18-ad45-591e-ab81-1483b9bbc230" :answer-field/choices ["answer-03661a97-3f4c-57e9-943b-6740f23533e0" "answer-24b2b15c-24e2-57bc-9b13-a06cbd4eb16e" "answer-aa458a18-ad45-591e-ab81-1483b9bbc230" "answer-7c88601f-7ff0-5a6b-af0b-a77dbae473cd" "answer-7335ea22-0c13-5b37-8b47-351229d967ef"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03661a97-3f4c-57e9-943b-6740f23533e0" :answer/id #uuid "03661a97-3f4c-57e9-943b-6740f23533e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{67}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24b2b15c-24e2-57bc-9b13-a06cbd4eb16e" :answer/id #uuid "24b2b15c-24e2-57bc-9b13-a06cbd4eb16e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{69}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa458a18-ad45-591e-ab81-1483b9bbc230" :answer/id #uuid "aa458a18-ad45-591e-ab81-1483b9bbc230" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{70}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c88601f-7ff0-5a6b-af0b-a77dbae473cd" :answer/id #uuid "7c88601f-7ff0-5a6b-af0b-a77dbae473cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{72}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7335ea22-0c13-5b37-8b47-351229d967ef" :answer/id #uuid "7335ea22-0c13-5b37-8b47-351229d967ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{73}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105739 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a323077c-5cf0-5ef0-a051-240e1171e494"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a323077c-5cf0-5ef0-a051-240e1171e494" :question/id #uuid "a323077c-5cf0-5ef0-a051-240e1171e494" :question/math-academy-id "q-52972" :question/problem "![](images/37/372ac1135e480bcd843f02b05bdeae42d462fccaced8151e4a355d6263d7be64.png)\n\nFind the value of $z$ in the triangle shown above." :question/worked-solution "First, from the diagram, notice that $∠CAB$ and $∠BAD$ are supplementary. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠CAB+m∠BAD & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠CAB+z & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠CAB & ={180}^{∘}-z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $△ABC$ is an isosceles triangle where $\\overset{―}{AB}≅\\overset{―}{BC}$, the base angles must be equal:\n\n$$\nm∠C=m∠CAB.\n$$\n\nFinally, since the interior angles of any triangle sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠CAB+m∠C+m∠B & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2m∠CAB+m∠B & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2({180}^{∘}-z)+{40}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {360}^{∘}-2z+{40}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2z & ={220}^{∘} \\\\ z & ={110}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2517a418-b87f-54f2-b710-d15c568a3534"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2517a418-b87f-54f2-b710-d15c568a3534" :answer-field/id #uuid "2517a418-b87f-54f2-b710-d15c568a3534" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f81ae10f-b2ec-5eff-a612-29b4fa814574" :answer-field/choices ["answer-46ca1c05-5190-5ad2-8c5c-d591894996c8" "answer-5274cb9d-d489-5332-8ddc-d0bf62c38087" "answer-f81ae10f-b2ec-5eff-a612-29b4fa814574" "answer-bfa840cd-3123-510e-bf31-113dff14f21e" "answer-f6ebedab-b10c-56a0-8c29-72fe32d8a4eb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46ca1c05-5190-5ad2-8c5c-d591894996c8" :answer/id #uuid "46ca1c05-5190-5ad2-8c5c-d591894996c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{107}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5274cb9d-d489-5332-8ddc-d0bf62c38087" :answer/id #uuid "5274cb9d-d489-5332-8ddc-d0bf62c38087" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{108}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f81ae10f-b2ec-5eff-a612-29b4fa814574" :answer/id #uuid "f81ae10f-b2ec-5eff-a612-29b4fa814574" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{110}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bfa840cd-3123-510e-bf31-113dff14f21e" :answer/id #uuid "bfa840cd-3123-510e-bf31-113dff14f21e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{112}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6ebedab-b10c-56a0-8c29-72fe32d8a4eb" :answer/id #uuid "f6ebedab-b10c-56a0-8c29-72fe32d8a4eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{113}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-7731ce61-1f9a-51e4-a49c-996258564f67" :activity/id #uuid "7731ce61-1f9a-51e4-a49c-996258564f67" :activity/title "The Isosceles Triangle Theorem" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049027 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-d4131835-327a-579d-bd13-775bb94299f0" "step-3970f23e-0d4b-58af-b62e-7ed9157998d2" "step-547a136f-0f45-5073-888d-a69eb3373469"] :activity/first-step "step-d4131835-327a-579d-bd13-775bb94299f0" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-d4131835-327a-579d-bd13-775bb94299f0" :step/id #uuid "d4131835-327a-579d-bd13-775bb94299f0" :step/content "question-b85bf70e-60cf-531c-93a8-54cd5e2b47c0" :step/next "step-3970f23e-0d4b-58af-b62e-7ed9157998d2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3970f23e-0d4b-58af-b62e-7ed9157998d2" :step/id #uuid "3970f23e-0d4b-58af-b62e-7ed9157998d2" :step/content "question-ae1938a1-58ee-571b-a544-d365ce409563" :step/next "step-547a136f-0f45-5073-888d-a69eb3373469" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-547a136f-0f45-5073-888d-a69eb3373469" :step/id #uuid "547a136f-0f45-5073-888d-a69eb3373469" :step/content "question-a323077c-5cf0-5ef0-a051-240e1171e494" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166752 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-edf4a097-cde0-5ac1-86d1-cd429ba599d0" "question-2e84799f-e1a6-5cc6-b626-825322837015"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-edf4a097-cde0-5ac1-86d1-cd429ba599d0" :question/id #uuid "edf4a097-cde0-5ac1-86d1-cd429ba599d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-95018" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 9 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 9 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 & 6{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2} & 3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}=8 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 & 8 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 & 8 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{3}{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{9}{2} & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}=8 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -\\frac{9}{2}{x}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=\\frac{2}{3}.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{1}+9\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} & =8 \\\\ 6{x}_{1} & =2 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-358ca9bd-a430-5e36-accd-2c83f3de20f2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-358ca9bd-a430-5e36-accd-2c83f3de20f2" :answer-field/id #uuid "358ca9bd-a430-5e36-accd-2c83f3de20f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fb160850-a523-56ec-9e9b-f5b031875117" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fb160850-a523-56ec-9e9b-f5b031875117" "answer-722274c3-742b-5a48-b51d-ae59fbe68344" "answer-991ed807-57db-5621-8684-6e0503cebcf6" "answer-107579c4-226c-56f4-a2e2-579b1beca778" "answer-e0e1b4b5-e50a-5c14-9473-88dec5bbe338"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb160850-a523-56ec-9e9b-f5b031875117" :answer/id #uuid "fb160850-a523-56ec-9e9b-f5b031875117" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-722274c3-742b-5a48-b51d-ae59fbe68344" :answer/id #uuid "722274c3-742b-5a48-b51d-ae59fbe68344" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-991ed807-57db-5621-8684-6e0503cebcf6" :answer/id #uuid "991ed807-57db-5621-8684-6e0503cebcf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-107579c4-226c-56f4-a2e2-579b1beca778" :answer/id #uuid "107579c4-226c-56f4-a2e2-579b1beca778" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0e1b4b5-e50a-5c14-9473-88dec5bbe338" :answer/id #uuid "e0e1b4b5-e50a-5c14-9473-88dec5bbe338" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167330 :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} & 7{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ -5{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}=-2 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 7 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 7 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{7}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}=-2 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ -{x}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=-1.$ \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-1+2=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186165189 :answer-field/correct 17592186165194 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166753 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2d45985d-1bef-55fa-a31c-73d51b4f78be" "question-881394e4-d1e2-502e-8f1c-cafafb97686c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2d45985d-1bef-55fa-a31c-73d51b4f78be" :question/id #uuid "2d45985d-1bef-55fa-a31c-73d51b4f78be" :question/math-academy-id "q-95029" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=-1-t+2{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t-{t}^{2},\\,q(t)=3-3t.\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(-1-t+2{t}^{2})+{x}_{2}(t-{t}^{2}) & =3-3t \\\\ -{x}_{1}+(-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})t+(2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}){t}^{2} & =3-3t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}=3 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first and second equations, we get ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=-6.$ \n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-3+(-6)=-9.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eef364c2-b743-5663-ae5b-bf40b13e0fd5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eef364c2-b743-5663-ae5b-bf40b13e0fd5" :answer-field/id #uuid "eef364c2-b743-5663-ae5b-bf40b13e0fd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-77f754b6-3412-584d-ba89-67035e23606c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e63f7738-750c-5af7-b550-1409a521290c" "answer-ba52f496-ec86-590f-89ec-2e6d908c3e02" "answer-77f754b6-3412-584d-ba89-67035e23606c" "answer-9749750d-293f-5863-817e-e6019efcfb73" "answer-a1d21a6a-0db9-5004-bce9-f0f22743dbc1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e63f7738-750c-5af7-b550-1409a521290c" :answer/id #uuid "e63f7738-750c-5af7-b550-1409a521290c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba52f496-ec86-590f-89ec-2e6d908c3e02" :answer/id #uuid "ba52f496-ec86-590f-89ec-2e6d908c3e02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77f754b6-3412-584d-ba89-67035e23606c" :answer/id #uuid "77f754b6-3412-584d-ba89-67035e23606c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9749750d-293f-5863-817e-e6019efcfb73" :answer/id #uuid "9749750d-293f-5863-817e-e6019efcfb73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1d21a6a-0db9-5004-bce9-f0f22743dbc1" :answer/id #uuid "a1d21a6a-0db9-5004-bce9-f0f22743dbc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2e84799f-e1a6-5cc6-b626-825322837015" :question/id #uuid "2e84799f-e1a6-5cc6-b626-825322837015" :question/math-academy-id "q-106779" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}\\},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 & {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=6 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=6 \\\\ {x}_{2}=4 \\\\ -{x}_{2}=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=4.$ From the first equation, we get  ${x}_{1}=6.$\n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=6+4=10.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d2e25b77-025f-5093-8bf8-7b6467b74964"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d2e25b77-025f-5093-8bf8-7b6467b74964" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2e25b77-025f-5093-8bf8-7b6467b74964" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-16f90a27-6313-5109-bbb8-4f7772524d5c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-16f90a27-6313-5109-bbb8-4f7772524d5c" "answer-9d32efd9-ca00-5319-9be6-643c6af3ff42" "answer-f157e119-b980-53fb-8f72-ef9064237542" "answer-2bd13daf-ca48-59e9-825a-a46dcf520048" "answer-bd09020a-ccf6-5dd6-a0c1-117aa3597348"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16f90a27-6313-5109-bbb8-4f7772524d5c" :answer/id #uuid "16f90a27-6313-5109-bbb8-4f7772524d5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d32efd9-ca00-5319-9be6-643c6af3ff42" :answer/id #uuid "9d32efd9-ca00-5319-9be6-643c6af3ff42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f157e119-b980-53fb-8f72-ef9064237542" :answer/id #uuid "f157e119-b980-53fb-8f72-ef9064237542" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2bd13daf-ca48-59e9-825a-a46dcf520048" :answer/id #uuid "2bd13daf-ca48-59e9-825a-a46dcf520048" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd09020a-ccf6-5dd6-a0c1-117aa3597348" :answer/id #uuid "bd09020a-ccf6-5dd6-a0c1-117aa3597348" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-881394e4-d1e2-502e-8f1c-cafafb97686c" :question/id #uuid "881394e4-d1e2-502e-8f1c-cafafb97686c" :question/math-academy-id "q-106782" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2-t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=3-2{t}^{2},\\,q(t)=3t-4{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf $B=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2-t)+{x}_{2}(3-2{t}^{2}) & =3t-4{t}^{2} \\\\ (2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2})-{x}_{1}t-2{x}_{2}{t}^{2} & =3t-4{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}=3 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}=3 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ From the  first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-3.$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-3+2=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ae5852dc-829f-545a-9915-7bda8a3606ff"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ae5852dc-829f-545a-9915-7bda8a3606ff" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae5852dc-829f-545a-9915-7bda8a3606ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e34854be-3584-5770-a376-eca2a97d5e2f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e34854be-3584-5770-a376-eca2a97d5e2f" "answer-b8494486-b6be-5318-969d-dd99f4d62997" "answer-c322b0fe-2579-53a9-a017-e308cf16a5b3" "answer-4beb3a66-909a-5284-8f19-4108f422c07d" "answer-d7634f67-a8f6-59d4-a750-b899dde278d6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e34854be-3584-5770-a376-eca2a97d5e2f" :answer/id #uuid "e34854be-3584-5770-a376-eca2a97d5e2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8494486-b6be-5318-969d-dd99f4d62997" :answer/id #uuid "b8494486-b6be-5318-969d-dd99f4d62997" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c322b0fe-2579-53a9-a017-e308cf16a5b3" :answer/id #uuid "c322b0fe-2579-53a9-a017-e308cf16a5b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4beb3a66-909a-5284-8f19-4108f422c07d" :answer/id #uuid "4beb3a66-909a-5284-8f19-4108f422c07d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7634f67-a8f6-59d4-a